{"qid":"Q244","names":["Barbados"],"title":"Barbados","endonym":{"native":"Barbados","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Barbados gained independence from Britain on 30 November 1966, with Errol Barrow as its first prime minister, becoming a constitutional monarchy with Elizabeth II as head of state. For over five decades it was one of the most stable parliamentary democracies in the Caribbean, with a per-capita income driven by tourism and financial services that placed it in the upper tier of developing nations. On 30 November 2021, exactly 55 years after independence, Barbados became a republic within the Commonwealth, with Dame Sandra Mason inaugurated as its first president, removing the British monarch as head of state.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Barbados is a fully sovereign island state; its territory—the island of Barbados at 431 km²—is precisely defined and uncontested.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Barbados","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbados"},{"label":"Britannica: Barbados","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Barbados"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Errol Barrow","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Errol_Barrow"}],"britannica":"place/Barbados","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Barbados","rulers":[{"qid":"Q9682","name":"Elizabeth II","start":1966,"end":2021,"image":"Queen Elizabeth II official portrait for 1959 tour (retouched) (cropped) (3-to-4 aspect ratio).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Queen%20Elizabeth%20II%20official%20portrait%20for%201959%20tour%20(retouched)%20(cropped)%20(3-to-4%20aspect%20ratio).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"lice